Keeps astro data under control — the full storage lifecycle (squash, ship, retain) of every camera stream as one system.

Owns the full storage lifecycle of the astro data streams (astrocam, eclipticam, starcam, skycam) as **one unified system**: (1) data-size reduction by squashing — temporal-resolution reduction + spatial sum8/sum2, the primary lever against t² cost growth; (2) disk management — ship-and-free per stream, no pressure-based GC (retired 2026-07-01); (3) Glacier Deep Archive of reduced/keeper nights. Retention is a *resolution schedule*, not keep-vs-delete: recent nights at full cadence, older nights progressively squashed, squashed form kept ~forever (the RRD pyramid → O(1) storage). The truth surface is the `/astro/storage` page. The opposite model to [[gardencam]]'s disposable-raw streams, which is why they're separate.
